<td id="S3.T1.6.1.20.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T1.6.1.20.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.554</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Evaluate stage analyzes the current retrieval outcome and converts it into structured feedback for subsequent reformulation. For each newly retrieved document <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> that has not been assessed before, a relevance assessor assigns a graded label:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}(q,d)=\mathcal{J}_{\phi}(q,d)\in\{0,1,2,3\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}(q,d)=\mathcal{J}_{\phi}(q,d)\in\{0,1,2,3\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the assessor, including the underlying LLM, prompt, and decoding configuration. Relevance is always assessed with respect to the original query <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, rather than the reformulated query <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. This keeps feedback anchored to the user’s information need and prevents reformulation drift from propagating across rounds.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{t-1}=\bigcup_{i=1}^{t-1}D_{i}^{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>new</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{t-1}=\bigcup_{i=1}^{t-1}D_{i}^{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the documents assessed before round <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. At each iteration, the assessor considers the top <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> documents in <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> that have not yet received a relevance label:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t}^{\mathrm{new}}=\{d\in\mathcal{L}_{t}\setminus\mathcal{S}_{t-1}\mid\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal{L}_{t}}(d)\leq K\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>new</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>rank</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t}^{\mathrm{new}}=\{d\in\mathcal{L}_{t}\setminus\mathcal{S}_{t-1}\mid\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal{L}_{t}}(d)\leq K\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The resulting assessments are incorporated into the feedback pool according to</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}=\mathcal{F}_{t-1}\cup\{(d,\hat{y}(q,d)):d\in D_{t}^{\mathrm{new}}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>new</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}=\mathcal{F}_{t-1}\cup\{(d,\hat{y}(q,d)):d\in D_{t}^{\mathrm{new}}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">As the iterative process progresses, <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> accumulates an increasingly rich set of graded relevance assessments that characterize which retrieval patterns consistently align with the information need and which contribute to retrieval drift. Because relevance is always evaluated against the original query <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, a document’s relevance label remains stable across rounds, eliminating the need for reassessment and allowing the computational budget to focus entirely on newly surfaced evidence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.2.4 </span>Iterative Refinement and Adaptive Termination</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The adapt–observe–evaluate cycle repeats across rounds, with each iteration refining the expansion using an updated feedback pool. Instead of running for a fixed number of rounds, <span id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ADORE</span> uses adaptive termination to allocate more computation to harder queries. The loop stops when one of three conditions is met: (i) <em id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">quality saturation</em>, where all assessed documents in the current round receive the maximum relevance score; (ii) <em id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">coverage saturation</em>, where the number of newly retrieved documents <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{t}^{\mathrm{new}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>new</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{t}^{\mathrm{new}}|</annotation></semantics></math> falls below a threshold <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for two consecutive rounds; or (iii) <em id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">budget exhaustion</em>, where the round counter reaches the maximum <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">After termination at round <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, final retrieval is performed using <math id="S3.SS2.SSS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{T^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{T^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since later pseudo-passages are generated from richer feedback, the final query uses the most refined expansion produced by the framework.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experimental Setup</h2>

<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
